window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-8531f28e6406b574"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"run-your-first-security-scan\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">运行首次安全扫描</h1> <p>查找代码中的漏洞、审查证据，并决定哪些问题需要处理。</p> <p>使用 Codex Security 插件扫描本地代码库，审查证据与覆盖范围，并确定哪些发现需要调查或修复。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>评估自己拥有或获准审查的代码库或服务的开发人员。</li> <li>正在建立漏洞初步概况，并查找需要进一步审查区域的安全团队。</li> <li>在决定修复方案前，需要代码证据和验证结果的审查人员。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-52ffdad46ad27a2b\">$codex-security:security-scan</a></td> <td>扫描代码库或指定文件夹，验证候选漏洞，并报告发现和覆盖范围。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>在代码库中查找漏洞</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>xhigh</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用 $codex-security:security-scan 对 [absolute path to this repository or one scoped folder]（此代码仓库或某个指定文件夹的绝对路径）运行标准安全扫描。\n\n我已获准评估此代码。请将审查严格限制在选定范围内。\n遵循代码库的安全指导和受支持的验证命令。\n不要应用修复，也不要关闭发现项。\n\n返回扫描报告，并总结：\n\n- 发现的问题、受影响代码及现实影响。\n- 验证证据和仍存在的不确定性。\n- 已审查区域、排除项和未完成的覆盖范围。\n- 需要先由人工审查的发现和覆盖缺口。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-bec1e26cb654a758\">安装 Codex Security 插件</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-52ffdad46ad27a2b?anchor=configure-the-scan\">扫描设置和推荐模型</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f8889c3a5e0f278c\">修复安全扫描中的发现项</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>使用 Codex Security 插件扫描本地代码库，审查每项发现的证据，并决定哪些问题需要调查或修复。先扫描一个代码库或服务，审查覆盖范围后再扩大扫描范围。</p> <p><a id=\"before-you-start\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">开始前</h2> <p>在 Codex 中打开一个你拥有或获准评估的本地代码库。安装并启用 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/security/plugin\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex Security 插件（需联网）</a>，并确认你的账户和工作区具备所需的<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/cyber-safety\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">安全访问权限（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>先对整个代码库或一个服务运行标准扫描。它会运行一次扫描工作流，并提供发现项、支持证据和覆盖范围，供你在决定修复方式前审查。对于大型单体仓库，选择一个服务或产品边界清楚的文件夹。</p> <p>在该仓库对应的 Codex 项目中使用起步提示词，并把路径替换为你想扫描的范围。若要在 Security 侧边栏中配置相同的扫描，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-8531f28e6406b574?anchor=run-your-first-scan\">运行首次扫描</a>。选择其中一种方式启动扫描。</p> <p><a id=\"run-your-first-scan\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">运行首次扫描</h2> <ol> <li>打开 <strong>Security（安全）</strong>，选择 <strong>Scans（扫描）</strong>，然后选择 <strong>+ Scan（新增扫描）</strong>。</li> <li>选择代码库，并确认 <strong>Current branch（当前分支）</strong> 和 <strong>Last commit（最近提交）</strong> 与要审查的代码一致。<strong>Codebase（代码库）</strong> 会扫描当前检出的代码，包括本地改动。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Codebase（代码库）</strong>，并将 <strong>Scan area（扫描区域）</strong> 设为 <strong>Entire codebase（整个代码库）</strong> 或某个文件夹。首次扫描请保持 Deep scan（深度扫描）关闭。</li> <li>根据当前<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/security/plugin/scans#configure-the-scan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">扫描建议（需联网）</a>选择模型和推理力度。</li> <li>如果要说明需优先处理的安全规则或区域，请打开 <strong>Additional context（补充背景）</strong>，然后选择 <strong>Start scan（开始扫描）</strong>。</li> </ol> <p>如果应用将每个客户的数据保存在独立工作区中，可以添加以下安全背景：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Users must only retrieve documents from workspaces they belong to.\nReview whether a user can supply another workspace's identifier and\nretrieve its private documents. Check where workspace membership is\nenforced, including background jobs and direct API calls.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">用户只能读取自己所属工作区中的文档。\n请审查用户是否可以提供另一个工作区的标识符，并读取其中的私有文档。检查工作区成员资格在何处得到强制验证，包括后台任务和直接 API 调用。</div></div> <figcaption> 安全文档中的扫描设置示例。开始扫描前，请确认你自己的代码库、范围和设置。 </figcaption> <p><a id=\"follow-the-scan-and-check-coverage\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">跟踪扫描并检查覆盖范围</h2> <p>Codex 会识别应用资产和安全边界，检查代码以发现候选漏洞，验证候选项，并评估其影响，然后生成报告。选择 <strong>View activity（查看活动）</strong> 查看底层 Codex 任务，并等待扫描完成。</p> <p>打开已完成的扫描，确认目标和修订版本。阅读发现项之前，先审查覆盖范围，包括跳过或延后的区域。扫描完成后仍可能发现漏洞；如果发现项列表为空但覆盖范围不完整，也不能据此证明代码安全。</p> <p>如果扫描停止或留下缺口，请记录这些区域以便后续跟进。扫描耗时和资源使用取决于所选代码及所需的验证工作。</p> <p><a id=\"understand-a-finding\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">理解一项发现</h2> <p>选择一项发现并打开 <strong>Summary（摘要）</strong>。结合以下问题进行审查：</p> <ul> <li><strong>攻击者能做什么？</strong> 阅读受影响代码、根本原因和报告的影响。</li> <li><strong>攻击者如何触达它？</strong> 从攻击者可控的输入追踪到敏感操作，并检查沿途已有的防护措施。</li> <li><strong>扫描实际证明了什么？</strong> 阅读验证证据、严重性判断理由和仍存在的不确定性。不能仅凭严重性标签就接受一项发现。</li> </ul> <figcaption> 安全文档中的发现示例，并非运行本演练所得的结果。 </figcaption> <p>在这个示例中，请求提供了一个工作区标识符；该标识符最终用于检索私有文档，却没有经过成员资格检查。评估代码中的类似发现时，请检查是否有其他控制措施强制要求成员资格，以及验证是否证明了跨工作区访问。</p> <p>若需协助解读某项发现，可在同一个仓库项目中打开聊天，并提供发现标题、受影响代码和证据：</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Help me assess this security finding: [paste the finding, affected code, and validation evidence].\n\nExplain the attack path, existing safeguards, and whether the evidence supports the reported impact and severity. Cite the relevant code and identify missing information. Do not modify code or close the finding.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请帮我评估这项安全发现：[paste the finding, affected code, and validation evidence]。\n\n解释攻击路径、现有防护，以及证据是否支持所报告的影响和严重程度。引用相关代码，指出缺失的信息。不要修改代码，也不要关闭这项发现。</div></div> <p><a id=\"choose-the-next-action\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">选择下一步</h2> <p>为每项已审查的发现简要记录：扫描的修订版本、受影响代码、证据、仍存在的不确定性和负责团队。根据证据选择下一步：</p> <ul> <li><strong>需要修复：</strong> 选择一项已确认的发现，继续<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/use-cases/fix-a-finding-from-your-security-scan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">修复安全扫描中的发现项（需联网）</a>。</li> <li><strong>需要调查：</strong> 保持发现项处于打开状态，并在决定修复方案前找出缺失的检查或信息。</li> <li><strong>不需要修复：</strong> 记录支持证据和分流决定。关闭发现项只表示记录了该决定，并不会更改代码。</li> </ul> <p>最终结果应是一组已审查的发现及覆盖缺口，并为每项注明下一步。如果需要更全面的评估，请使用<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/use-cases/deep-security-scan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">运行深度安全扫描（需联网）</a>。如果要评估特定拉取请求或差异，请使用<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/use-cases/scan-code-changes-for-security\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">扫描代码更改（需联网）</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"run-your-first-security-scan\">Run your first security scan</h1> <p>Find vulnerabilities in your code, review the evidence, and decide what needs attention.</p> <p>Use the Codex Security plugin to scan a local repository, review the evidence and coverage, and prioritize findings for investigation or a fix.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Developers assessing a repository or service they own or are authorized to review.</li> <li>Security teams establishing an initial view of vulnerabilities and areas that need further review.</li> <li>Reviewers who need code evidence and validation results before deciding what to fix.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-52ffdad46ad27a2b\">$codex-security:security-scan</a></td> <td>Scan a repository or scoped folder, validate candidate vulnerabilities, and report findings and coverage.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Find vulnerabilities in a repository</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>xhigh</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:security-scan to run a standard security scan of [absolute path to this repository or one scoped folder].\n\nI am authorized to assess this code. Keep the review within the selected scope.\nUse the repository's security guidance and supported validation commands.\nDo not apply fixes or close findings.\n\nReturn the scan report and summarize:\n- Findings, affected code, and realistic impact.\n- Validation evidence and remaining uncertainty.\n- Reviewed areas, exclusions, and incomplete coverage.\n- Findings and coverage gaps that need human review first.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-bec1e26cb654a758\">Install the Codex Security plugin</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-52ffdad46ad27a2b?anchor=configure-the-scan\">Scan settings and recommended model</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f8889c3a5e0f278c\">Fix a finding from your security scan</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Scan a local repository with the Codex Security plugin, review the evidence behind each finding, and decide what needs investigation or a fix. Start with one repository or service so you can review its coverage before expanding the scan.</p> <h2 id=\"before-you-start\">Before you start</h2> <p>Open a local repository that you own or have permission to assess in Codex. Install and enable the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/security/plugin\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex Security plugin (online)</a>, and confirm that your account and workspace have the required <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/cyber-safety\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">security access (online)</a>.</p> <p>Start with a standard scan of the repository or one service. It runs the scan workflow once and gives you findings, supporting evidence, and coverage to review before deciding what to fix. For a large monorepo, choose one folder with a clear service or product boundary.</p> <p>Use the starter prompt in that repository's Codex project, replacing the path with your intended scope. To configure the same scan in the Security sidebar, follow <a href=\"#/article/a-8531f28e6406b574?anchor=run-your-first-scan\">Run your first scan</a>. Choose one way to start the scan.</p> <h2 id=\"run-your-first-scan\">Run your first scan</h2> <ol> <li>Open <strong>Security</strong>, select <strong>Scans</strong>, then select <strong>+ Scan</strong>.</li> <li>Select your repository and confirm that <strong>Current branch</strong> and <strong>Last commit</strong> match the code you want to review. <strong>Codebase</strong> scans the checked-out code, including local changes.</li> <li>Select <strong>Codebase</strong> and set <strong>Scan area</strong> to <strong>Entire codebase</strong> or one folder. Leave <strong>Deep scan</strong> off for this first pass.</li> <li>Choose a model and reasoning effort using the current <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/security/plugin/scans#configure-the-scan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">scan recommendations (online)</a>.</li> <li>Open <strong>Additional context</strong> if you want to explain a security rule or area to prioritize, then select <strong>Start scan</strong>.</li> </ol> <p>For an application that keeps each customer's data in a separate workspace, you could add this security context:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Users must only retrieve documents from workspaces they belong to.\nReview whether a user can supply another workspace's identifier and\nretrieve its private documents. Check where workspace membership is\nenforced, including background jobs and direct API calls.\n</code></pre> <figcaption> Example scan setup from the security docs. Confirm your own repository, scope, and settings before starting. </figcaption> <h2 id=\"follow-the-scan-and-check-coverage\">Follow the scan and check coverage</h2> <p>Codex identifies the application's assets and security boundaries, reviews code for candidate vulnerabilities, validates candidates, and assesses their impact before producing the report. Select <strong>View activity</strong> to inspect the underlying Codex task, and wait for the scan to finish.</p> <p>Open the completed scan and confirm the target and revision. Review coverage, including skipped or deferred areas, before reading the findings. A completed scan can contain vulnerabilities; an empty findings list with incomplete coverage does not establish that the code is secure.</p> <p>If the scan stops or leaves gaps, record those areas for follow-up. Scan time and resource use depend on the selected code and the validation work required.</p> <h2 id=\"understand-a-finding\">Understand a finding</h2> <p>Select a finding and open <strong>Summary</strong>. Review these questions together:</p> <ul> <li><strong>What can an attacker do?</strong> Read the affected code, root cause, and reported impact.</li> <li><strong>How can they reach it?</strong> Follow the attack path from attacker-controlled input to the sensitive operation, including any existing safeguards.</li> <li><strong>What did the scan demonstrate?</strong> Read the validation evidence, severity rationale, and remaining uncertainty. A severity label alone is not enough to accept a finding.</li> </ul> <figcaption> Example finding from the security docs, not the result of running this walkthrough. </figcaption> <p>In this example, a request supplies a workspace identifier that reaches private-document retrieval without a membership check. To assess a similar finding in your code, inspect whether another control enforces membership and whether the validation demonstrates access across workspaces.</p> <p>For help interpreting a finding, open a chat in the same repository project and include the finding's title, affected code, and evidence:</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Help me assess this security finding: [paste the finding, affected code, and validation evidence].\n\nExplain the attack path, existing safeguards, and whether the evidence supports the reported impact and severity. Cite the relevant code and identify missing information. Do not modify code or close the finding.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"choose-the-next-action\">Choose the next action</h2> <p>Keep a short record of each reviewed finding: the scanned revision, affected code, evidence, remaining uncertainty, and responsible team. Choose the next action based on that evidence:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Needs a fix:</strong> Select one accepted finding and continue to <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/use-cases/fix-a-finding-from-your-security-scan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Fix a finding from your security scan (online)</a>.</li> <li><strong>Needs investigation:</strong> Keep it open and identify the missing check or information before making a remediation decision.</li> <li><strong>Does not need a fix:</strong> Record the supporting evidence and your triage decision. Closing a finding records that decision; it does not change code.</li> </ul> <p>Your result is a reviewed set of findings and coverage gaps, with a next action for each. If you need a more thorough assessment, use <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/use-cases/deep-security-scan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Run a deep security scan (online)</a>. To assess a specific pull request or diff, use <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/use-cases/scan-code-changes-for-security\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Scan code changes for security (online)</a>.</p>"};
